    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green (45 tests, 0 failures) including the new `Cp31Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `checkDigit` as a derived, read-only field \u2014 a single Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode`.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n2. **`CustomerCodeCheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper (mirroring `OwnerIdentityKey`) computing the Luhn check digit over the digits in `customerCode`, ignoring the dashes; returns `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`.\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression populating `checkDigit` from `owner.getCustomerCode()`.\n\nBecause the check digit is a pure function of `customerCode`, it's computed at read time in the mapper alongside the other derived fields (`initials`, `identityKey`, `membershipLevel`) rather than needing a new pipeline step. The logic matches the test's independent `luhn()` implementation, so `Cp31Tests.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes.",
